            <ArticleTitle>Aneurysm of the mitral-aortic intervalvular fibrosa as a rare cause of angina pectoris: angiographic demonstration.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>423-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Aneurysms of the mitral-aortic interventricular fibrosa (MAIF) are exceptionally rare complications, commonly following aortic valve endocarditis. This report describes the angiographic findings of such an aneurysm, in a patient who developed an uncommon symptomatology of unstable angina pectoris, caused by the aneurysm's expansion against the coronary arteries. Surgical treatment is also discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
